    "updated_at": "2020-08-26T18:25:16Z",
    "body": "@jescalan can you grep your configs for `brew --prefix`? I just came across starship and before I install any software, I try to see what some of the glaring issues are first. There's a version manager called asdf that I use and by process of deduction (removing everything in configs and then adding each thing back), I discovered Homebrew to be the culprit in introducing seconds into my prompt. You can view my issue that was subsequently addressed by a maintainer here: https://github.com/asdf-vm/asdf/issues/771\r\n\r\nI spent a quick couple minutes doing a quick search for references to `brew --prefix` in this repo as well as the Homebrew formula and didn't find anything (didn't expect to), because it's something that was added by me from the suggestion in their documentation. If you visit my link, you can probably find the culprit the same way. \r\n\r\nWhen I have time to test-drive starship, I can report back on whether or not it affects me, but I don't want to be screwing around with my prompt right now",
    "author_association": "NONE",
