    "updated_at": "2020-10-13T20:57:46Z",
    "body": "Slowness seems to be specifically with the `git_status` module.  Timings to execute `time starship prompt` for me with `git_status` enabled with the default settings:\r\n```\r\nreal    0m5.778s\r\nuser    0m3.253s\r\nsys     0m2.724s\r\n```\r\nIf I disable `git_status` altogether:\r\n```\r\nreal    0m0.091s\r\nuser    0m0.042s\r\nsys     0m0.045s\r\n```\r\nThe particular repo that I am running this against has ~330 branches.  I suspect this is a factor because if I go to a repo with only a few branches, the execution time is more reasonable.\r\n\r\nMy environment:\r\n* starship: 0.46.0 (installed via Homebrew)\r\n* bash: 5.0.18\r\n* MacOS: 10.15.6\r\n* iTerm2: 3.3.11",
    "author_association": "NONE",
